"""Write journal figure legends and trace each previous/new panel to its data."""
from context_figure_common import *

def document(stage):
    src=stage/"04_figures/source_data"; out=stage/"03_results"
    f1=read(src/"F1_chen.tsv.gz");e1=f1[f1.row_type.eq("effect")].iloc[0]
    f2=read(src/"F2_cross_screen.tsv");e2=f2[f2.row_type.eq("effect")].iloc[0]
    r=read(src/"F3_foxp3_tcr.tsv").set_index("analysis")
    d=read(out/"R10_TREG_TCONV_PRIMARY.tsv").set_index("analysis").loc["discordant_primary"]
    cont=read(out/"R10_TREG_TCONV_CONTINUOUS.tsv").set_index("analysis").loc["abs_rank_mean"]
    a=read(out/"R10_TREG_TCONV_ADJUSTED.tsv").set_index("analysis")
    cond=a.loc["discordant_complete_case_conditioned_exact"];firth=a.loc["discordant_complete_case_Firth_adjusted"]
    h=read(out/"R10_HUMAN_EXPRESSION_PANEL.tsv");m=read(out/"R10_MOUSE_EXPRESSION_PANEL.tsv")
    hit=read(out/"R10_PERTURB_COVERAGE.tsv");pr=read(out/"R10_PERTURB_PROTEIN.tsv")
    nlibrary=sum(truth(hit.targeted_in_input_library));nscore=pr[pr.score.notna()].gene.nunique()
    text=f"""# Figure legends

## Figure 1. FOXP3 hit enrichment among ASD-associated genes in human induced Tregs

(A) Each symbol represents one of 18,966 measured genes in the Chen et al. induced regulatory T-cell (iTreg) screen. Axes give the source MAGeCK log fold change for the FOXP3-low versus FOXP3-high contrast and the negative base-10 logarithm of the smaller raw one-tailed P value. Gray circles denote other genes and open navy circles denote SFARI score-1 genes without a hit. The triangles identify score-1 hits at the author-derived FDR threshold of 0.05 in either tail. A downward teal triangle denotes lower FOXP3 after knockout and an upward orange triangle denotes higher FOXP3. (B) Hit rates were 14/242 among score-1 genes and 243/18,724 among other measured genes. The conditional odds ratio (OR) was {e1.effect:.2f} (two-sided exact 95% CI {e1.effect_low:.2f}–{e1.effect_high:.2f}, one-sided Fisher enrichment P = {e1.p:.6g}). (C) Nine of the 14 hits were associated with lower FOXP3 after knockout and five with higher FOXP3. Signed positions retain the same native low-versus-high axis as in A. The original study reported two screening replicates in cord-blood-derived iTregs. The donor relationship between the two replicates was unresolved. Source: Chen et al., Supplementary Table 1 (PMID 40140585).

## Figure 2. FOXP3 hits in primary human Tregs, gene attributes and loss-of-function direction

(A) Five of 33 measured score-1 genes and 26 of 1,316 other genes were hits in the Umhoefer primary-Treg assay (conditional OR {e2.effect:.2f}, two-sided exact 95% CI {e2.effect_low:.2f}–{e2.effect_high:.2f}, one-sided Fisher P = {e2.p:.6g}). (B) Of the 33 score-1 genes common to both assays, two were hits in both, three in primary Tregs only and 28 in neither. The panel displays all five genes with a hit in either screen. Triangles indicate the direction of knockout-associated FOXP3 change and open circles indicate measured nonhits. Twelve other Chen hits lay outside the targeted primary-Treg library. (C) Points and intervals show Firth ORs with two-sided 95% penalized profile-likelihood CIs. Within each screen the four models use the same CPM ≥1 complete cases, 10,463 Chen genes (173 score-1) and 698 Umhoefer genes (18 score-1). M0 includes the score-1 indicator. M1 adds transcription-factor and EpiFactors membership and, for Chen, membership in the targeted library. The primary M2 model adds continuous expression and LOEUF. M3 further adds genomic span and guide count. Chen uses the iTreg non-targeting-guide expression reference and Umhoefer uses the expanded hTreg expression reference. Filled symbols denote M2, with two-screen Holm P = 0.360 and 0.101, respectively. (D) Four one-sided, stratum-conditioned directional tests in the prespecified loss-of-function-compatible subset are summarized as observed/expected hit counts. Lower and higher refer to FOXP3 after knockout. Holm adjustment covers both directions in both screens. The strict populations retained 74/103 measured eligible genes in Chen and 7/19 in primary Tregs. Zero is the observed ratio for primary-Treg FOXP3-increasing hits. The observed/expected ratios have no model-based effect intervals. Sources: Chen et al. (PMID 40140585) and Umhoefer et al. (GSE286470, PMID 41237776).

## Figure 3. Comparisons across FOXP3 and proliferation phenotypes and between FOXP3 cell contexts

(A) The Chen iTreg FOXP3 and Shifrut TCR-stimulated proliferation screens shared 18,615 measured genes (242 score-1). In the full shared universe, FOXP3-only, proliferation-only, both-hit and neither-hit classes contained 179, 874, 78 and 17,484 genes, respectively. The corresponding score-1 counts were 11, eight, three and 220. The observed signed preference was 11 − 8 = +3. Curves show exact null probability on the displayed support. The directional upper-tail probabilities use the full distributions. The complete-case conditioned curve (11,206 genes, 189 score-1) fixes class, targeted-library membership, expression and LOEUF strata. Its actual observed score was also +3, with one-sided exact P = {r.loc['COMPLETE_CASE_CONDITIONED','raw_P']:.5f}, compared with {r.loc['FULL_MEASURED_UNADJUSTED','raw_P']:.7f} in the full measured comparison. (B) Among 930 complete-case discordant genes (19 score-1), Firth logistic regression estimates the score-1-associated odds of a FOXP3-only hit. Covariate adjustment gave OR {r.loc['DISCORDANT_ADJUSTED_FIRTH','OR']:.2f} (95% profile CI {r.loc['DISCORDANT_ADJUSTED_FIRTH','CI_low']:.2f}–{r.loc['DISCORDANT_ADJUSTED_FIRTH','CI_high']:.2f}, two-sided penalized likelihood P = {r.loc['DISCORDANT_ADJUSTED_FIRTH','raw_P']:.5f}). (C) The primary Treg and activated Tconv assays measured 1,349 common genes, including 33 score-1 genes. The two-sided exact Fisher test compares score-1 and other genes on Treg-only versus Tconv-only membership within the {int(d.n)} discordant genes (OR {d.OR:.2f}, 95% exact CI {d.CI_low:.3f}–{d.CI_high:.2f}, P = {d.P:.5f}). The corresponding property-conditioned exact P was {cond.P:.3f}. The adjusted Firth sensitivity gave OR {firth.OR:.2f} (95% profile CI {firth.CI_low:.2f}–{firth.CI_high:.2f}, P = {firth.P:.4f}). (D) The empirical curves show each gene’s within-screen absolute-effect midrank percentile in Tregs minus its percentile in Tconvs. The score-1-minus-other mean difference was {cont.effect:+.4f} (gene bootstrap 95% CI {cont.CI_low:+.4f} to {cont.CI_high:+.4f}, {int(cont.B):,} label permutations, two-sided P = {cont.P:.5f}, Monte Carlo SE = {cont.mc_se:.5f}). The interval and P value use separate procedures. The Treg assay had two donor labels and the Tconv assay three. Donor pairing across assays was unresolved. Sources: Chen et al. (PMID 40140585), Shifrut et al. (PMID 30449619) and Umhoefer et al. (PMID 41237776).

## Figure 4. Cross-immune expression breadth and perturbation-associated protein scores

(A) The 14 fixed Chen discovery hits and four reference genes are shown for all 29 sorted human blood immune types in GSE107011. Colors give log₂(TPM + 1) after summarizing expression by the median of available donors within each type. The 114 sorted libraries represent four donors. Terminal effector CD4 cells have two donor measurements. The white rule separates the reference genes. (B) Each label gives the number of cell types detected divided by the number evaluated. Bars count candidate genes with that breadth. Human detection required a cell-type median of at least 1 TPM. Of the 14 genes, 13 were detected in all 29 types and KDM6B in 28. Mouse detection required at least 1 TMM-normalized CPM per group. All 14 one-to-one orthologs were detected in all 56 baseline groups (115 libraries). The two panels of source data retain their original species-specific units. (C) Chen et al. included {nlibrary} candidates in the initial Perturb-icCITE-seq library. {nscore} have protein scores in Supplementary Table 2. The heatmap shows the four measured reference markers for these {nscore} targets. CD25 corresponds to IL2RA and Helios to IKZF2. Each author's score equals the mean protein measurement in targeted cells minus its non-targeting control mean, divided by the control mean. A value of zero corresponds to the control baseline. The score describes a protein readout in the follow-up experiment. Supplementary Figures S12–S13 show all 88 assays for these candidates. Sources: Monaco et al. (GSE107011, PMID 30726743), ImmGen ULI (GSE109125, Yoshida et al., PMID 30686579) and Chen et al. (PMID 40140585).
"""
    (stage/"04_figures/R10_FIGURE_LEGENDS_EN.md").write_text(text)
    panelmap=[
        ("1A","1A","Whole-genome iTreg screen","04_figures/source_data/F1_chen.tsv.gz","screen_gene: native LFC, strength, score1, author hit, standardized direction","Retain all measured genes."),
        ("1B","1B","iTreg enrichment","04_figures/source_data/F1_chen.tsv.gz","enrichment: margins and conditional OR/CI/P","Retain frozen estimate."),
        ("1C","1C","14 effects","04_figures/source_data/F1_chen.tsv.gz","14 score-1 screen hits: native LFC","Order by native LFC, preserve all directions."),
        ("2A","2A","Primary Treg enrichment","04_figures/source_data/F2_cross_screen.tsv","enrichment: margins and conditional OR/CI/P","Retain targeted-library denominator."),
        ("2B/C","2B and legend; S1","Shared score-1 membership","04_figures/source_data/F2_cross_screen.tsv","common_asd_gene: both hit flags and directions","Display all five hits and give full 33-gene matrix in S1."),
        ("3D","2C","Firth M0–M3","04_figures/source_data/F2_models.tsv","model, screen, OR, CI_low, CI_high, holm_p_m2","Keep all eight frozen fits grouped with independent FOXP3 screen."),
        ("S13a table extension","2D","Directional LoF conditional O/E","04_figures/source_data/F2_lof.tsv","STRICT_CONDITIONAL_EXACT: effect, p_holm","Add all four directions including zero and nonsignificant estimates."),
        ("3A/B/C and S13b","3A","Exact FOXP3–proliferation preference","04_figures/source_data/F3_foxp3_tcr.tsv + F3_foxp3_tcr_null.tsv.gz","full and conditioned exact PMFs; observed S, N, A, raw_P","Preserve full-universe comparison and four-class counts in legend; overlay distinct conditional null."),
        ("S13b table extension","3B","Discordant Firth comparison","04_figures/source_data/F3_foxp3_tcr.tsv","DISCORDANT_UNADJUSTED_FIRTH and DISCORDANT_ADJUSTED_FIRTH; OR, CI_low/high, raw_P","Show discordant odds on their own scale."),
        ("New","3C","Primary Treg vs Tconv exclusive hits","04_figures/source_data/F3C_hit_classes.tsv + F3C_discordant_fisher.tsv","all four class counts and exact OR/CI/P","Show shared tested background."),
        ("New","3D","Continuous absolute-effect rank comparison","04_figures/source_data/F3D_rank_difference.tsv.gz + F3D_continuous_contrast.tsv","data-derived ECDF; group difference and interval/P","Include all tested genes."),
        ("New","4A and S8","Human immune expression","03_results/R10_MONACO_EXPRESSION_HEATMAP_SOURCE.tsv","log2_tpm_plus_1; row_z (S8)","All candidate and reference genes; all 29 types."),
        ("New","4B","Human and mouse breadth","04_figures/source_data/F4B_breadth.tsv","number of candidate genes per observed detected/evaluable fraction","Compare breadth descriptively in each atlas."),
        ("New","4C","Candidate protein changes","04_figures/source_data/F4C_protein_scores.tsv","author scores for all scored candidates and four reference proteins","Seven scored targets; all 88 protein assays in S12–S13."),
        ("4A/B/C","S7","Moreno patient Treg expression programs","04_figures/source_data/S7_moreno.tsv.gz","10 program coverage entries, five eligible estimates and four paired ECDFs with 5,851 feature rows","Migrate original vector artwork and legend in full."),
        ("S1–S6","S1–S6","Previous supplementary evidence","04_figures/source_data/FROZEN_FIGURE_INPUTS.tsv","embedded previously rendered vector page; source member hashes and plotted values retained","Preserve original page content and add a justified legend below each figure."),
        ("New","S9/S10","Mouse immune expression","03_results/R10_MOUSE_EXPRESSION_PLOT.tsv","log2_cpm1, zscore for 56 groups and 18 orthologs","Present baseline groups and reference genes, units specific to mouse."),
        ("New","S11","Donor-specific CD4 comparisons","03_results/R10_EXPRESSION_DONOR_CONTRASTS.tsv","primary_balanced_six: absolute paired values and four log2 contrasts per gene","Display donor-level expression estimates."),
        ("New","S12/S13","Protein perturbation scores","03_results/R10_PERTURB_PROTEIN.tsv","all scored candidates × 27 intracellular and 61 surface markers","Common complete score range across the companion figures."),
        ("New","S14","Treg expression ranks","03_results/R10_HUMAN_EXPRESSION_PANEL.tsv + R10_MOUSE_EXPRESSION_PANEL.tsv","treg_rank_desc, splenic_treg_rank, colonic_treg_rank","Separate species universes and mouse tissues.")]
    write(pd.DataFrame(panelmap,columns=["previous_panel","revision_panel","readout","source","selection_and_fields","reason"]),stage/"04_figures/R10_FIGURE_PANEL_MAP.tsv")
if __name__=="__main__":
    a=args();document(a.stage)
